From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:59:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] edid: give the 1400x1050 timing its size

The generator's mode table gives the established timing III of byte 8,
bit 1, the size 1440x1050, a mode no standard has; that bit is
1400x1050 at 60 Hz. The table's size decides whether a mode fits the
maximum and how it is offered. While a standard timing is free, a mode
that fits goes there or nowhere, and no standard timing has the aspect
ratio of 1440x1050: with a maximum that leaves one free when the table
reaches the entry - 1920x1200, 1920x1080, a width from 1400 to 1439 -
the mode was left out.

Give it its size. With such a maximum, 1400x1050 now takes a standard
timing. Where it takes the last one, as with 1920x1200, the timings III
now get 1360x768, which no standard timing can give and which was left
out too. Without a maximum, as for virtio-gpu, the standard timings are
full before the table reaches the entry, and the EDID is the same.

Fixes: 72d277a70e8b ("display/edid: add edid generator to qemu.")
Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 hw/display/edid-generate.c |  2 +-
 tests/unit/test-edid.c     | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/display/edid-generate.c b/hw/display/edid-generate.c
index af49e457be..0824580071 100644
--- a/hw/display/edid-generate.c
+++ b/hw/display/edid-generate.c
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ static const struct edid_mode {
     { .xres = 1920,   .yres = 1440,   .xtra3 = 11,   .bit = 5 },
     { .xres = 1856,   .yres = 1392,   .xtra3 = 10,   .bit = 3 },
     { .xres = 1792,   .yres = 1344,   .xtra3 = 10,   .bit = 5 },
-    { .xres = 1440,   .yres = 1050,   .xtra3 =  8,   .bit = 1 },
+    { .xres = 1400,   .yres = 1050,   .xtra3 =  8,   .bit = 1 },
     { .xres = 1360,   .yres =  768,   .xtra3 =  8,   .bit = 7 },
 
     /* established timings (all @ 60Hz) */
diff --git a/tests/unit/test-edid.c b/tests/unit/test-edid.c
index 82ea2f0c8d..8a81726e57 100644
--- a/tests/unit/test-edid.c
+++ b/tests/unit/test-edid.c
@@ -80,11 +80,35 @@ static void test_edid_text(void)
     g_assert_cmpstr(text, ==, "ABCDEFGHIJKLM");
 }
 
+/* Whether a standard timing of the base block is @xres at 60 Hz, 4:3. */
+static bool has_std_4_3(const uint8_t *edid, uint32_t xres)
+{
+    for (int i = 38; i < 54; i += 2) {
+        if (edid[i] == xres / 8 - 31 && edid[i + 1] == 0x40) {
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
+    return false;
+}
+
+/* A mode is offered when it fits the maximum, and one that does not, not. */
+static void test_edid_max(void)
+{
+    uint8_t edid[EDID_SIZE];
+    qemu_edid_info info = { .maxx = 1400, .maxy = 1050 };
+
+    generate(edid, sizeof(edid), &info);
+    g_assert_true(has_std_4_3(edid, 1400));
+    g_assert_true(has_std_4_3(edid, 1280));
+    g_assert_false(has_std_4_3(edid, 1600));
+}
+
 int main(int argc, char **argv)
 {
     g_test_init(&argc, &argv, NULL);
 
     g_test_add_func("/edid/text", test_edid_text);
+    g_test_add_func("/edid/max", test_edid_max);
 
     return g_test_run();
 }
